  "limitations": [
    "Ranks head CANDIDATES, the merge's input, not the merged shards.",
    "Candidate packs are ALREADY capped per map task, so a token's rows top out at tasks * HEAD_RESULT_CAP. A computed rank <= HEAD_RESULT_CAP is exact (that is the decomposability property the cap key is built on); a computed rank ABOVE it is a LOWER BOUND, because better-ranked siblings may have been dropped by their own task's cap. Read 'cap_needed_to_recover' above 10 as 'at least this much', never as a sufficient cap.",
    "Query tokenization mirrors the producer's word normalization; it is not the Worker's tokenizer executed in-process.",
    "A cap raise is scored as recovery only if the record survives in EVERY queried token, since the head intersects per-token lists."
